# INTENTIONALLY EMPTY - no Sink is registered by this module.
#
# SqsSink used to be listed here, "pre-registered for future auto-config".
# It was removed in sprint-23 (Story 1.2) for the same two reasons as its
# GCP twin (see the gcp-pubsub module's Sink file):
#
#  1. NOT CONSTRUCTIBLE. Its only constructor takes (SqsClient, queueUrl)
#     (SqsSink.java:71), so ServiceLoader raised ServiceConfigurationError
#     on every discovery pass. AutoConfig swallowed that error before
#     Story 1.1.
#
#  2. Sink IS NOT A ONE-PER-CLASSPATH CONTRACT. AutoConfig exposes no
#     singular sink() accessor, only the plural sinks()
#     (AutoConfig.java:268-270). A queue URL is per-stage wiring, not
#     per-environment configuration, so there is no honest no-arg
#     constructor to write.
#
# Story 1.2 AC 5 scoped the AWS entries as "fix only if it is a genuine
# no-arg constructor; otherwise leave the registration removed and flag
# it". It is not, so this is the removal branch.
#
# The class is unchanged and fully supported. Construct it per stage:
#     new SqsSink(client, queueUrl)
